 Carbon/Toolbox

                  NOTE: When run in non-command line environments, the
                        Carbon/Toolbox versions of MyMan read
                        environment variable overrides and default
                        command-line arguments from the 'STR#'
                        resource IDs 128 "envp" and 129 "argv",
                        respectively. These values can be set using
                        ResEdit for stand-alone Carbon CFM/Toolbox
                        binaries, or by compiling resources into the
                        data fork of the
                        myman.app/Contents/Resources/myman.rsrc file
                        for bundled Mac OS X Carbon Mach-O
                        applications. For example, to reduce the
                        default font size to 9, use raw tile
                        characters and rotate the display, create a
                        file "smallfont.r" with these contents:

  type'STR#'{integer=$$countof(_);array _{pstring;};};
  resource'STR#'(128,"envp"){{"MACCURSES_FONTSIZE=9"}};
  resource'STR#'(129,"argv"){{"-r","-x"}};

                        Compile the resource into the resource
                        file in a bundled Mac OS X Carbon Mach-O
                        application:

  Rez -useDF -a -o myman.app/Contents/Resources/myman.rsrc smallfont.r

                        For standalone Carbon CFM/Toolbox binaries
                        compile the resource into the application
                        binary's resource fork:

  Rez -a -o carbon-smallman smallfont.r

                        The changes should be visible at the next
                        launch of the application.

                        MACCURSES_FONT      Font name
                        MACCURSES_FONTSIZE  Initial font size in pixels
                        MACCURSES_FONTENCODING
                                            Font encoding name, possibly one of:
                                                CP437
                                                MacRoman
                                                MacJapanese
                                                MacVT100
                                                US-ASCII
                        OPTCURSES_DIRECT    Nonzero value disables redraw
                                            optimization layer
                        OPTCURSES_INTERLACE Nonzero value renders by
                                            interleaving half-screens
                        OPTCURSES_BITMAP    Nonzero value causes use of
                                            pseudo-bitmap characters
                        OPTCURSES_BITMAP_FORCE
                                            Nonzero value allows use of
                                            inverse video when using
                                            ASCII pseudo-bitmap characters
                        OPTCURSES_BITMAP_BRAILLE
                                            Nonzero value forces use of
                                            Braille pseudo-bitmap characters
                                            on a Unicode display
                        OPTCURSES_TALL      Nonzero value allows use
                                            of the VT100 double-width,
                                            double-height characters by
                                            doubling each row.

